    </tr>
    <tr style="height:31.7pt;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;">
     <td style="padding-top:0in;text-indent:2.5pt;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0in;text-align:left;"><p style="margin-left:0.467%;text-indent:0;font-size:12pt;margin-top:4.55pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Tristan Gerra</font></p><p style="margin-left:0.467%;text-indent:0;font-size:8pt;margin-top:1.1pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#6e6e6e;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Analyst, Robert W. Baird &amp; Co., Inc.</font></p></td>
     <td style="padding-top:0in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0in;text-align:center;"><p style="font-size:28pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:0.444%;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#a6a6a6;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Q</font></p></td>
     <td style="padding-top:0in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0in;text-align:center;"><p style="font-size:28pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:0.444%;text-align:right;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
    </tr>
   </table><p style="margin-left:3.333%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:2.9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:6.139%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Okay, great. And then just as a quick follow-up. So, you've mentioned capacity expansion efforts, is that on the front-end, is that internal capacity, and if so, in what geography are you building capacity?</font></p>
   <table style="margin-left:2.935%;border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:94.0%;border-collapse:separate;">
    <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
     <td style="width:64.38%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
     <td style="width:35.62%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="height:31.7pt;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;">
     <td style="padding-top:0in;text-indent:2.5pt;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0in;text-align:left;"><p style="margin-left:0.467%;text-indent:0;font-size:12pt;margin-top:4.55pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gary Yu</font></p><p style="margin-left:0.467%;text-indent:0;font-size:8pt;margin-top:1.1pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#6e6e6e;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-style:italic;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">President, Chief Executive Officer &amp; Director, Diodes, Inc.</font></p></td>
     <td style="padding-top:0in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0in;text-align:center;"><p style="font-size:28pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:0.444%;text-align:right;"><font style="color:#a6a6a6;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">A</font></p></td>
    </tr>
   </table><p style="margin-left:3.333%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:2.9pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:3.972%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Well, let me say that in this way. Okay. For the wafer fab, we continue utilizing improving the utilization for our GFAB and SPFAB, and there's some room we can also &#x2013; we can do more on that. And also we're doing some migration from 6-inch to 8-inch, right, to get more capacity on the wafer fab. Also leverage our external partner right and no matter if that partner is in Korea or in Thailand to get more capacity from them. So that's one thing. Secondly is therefore our assembly/testing, probably 75% of assembly/testing we do internally. On the particular</font></p></div>
